id: ble_unified
package: bluetooth_le_siwx91x
description: >
  BLE Unified Component - Minimal orchestration layer for BLE protocol components.
  Provides event loop coordination, protocol initialization orchestration, and power save management.
  Protocol-specific functionality is handled by separate protocol components (GAP, GATT, SMP, Advertising).
label: BLE Unified
category: Device|Si91x|Wireless
quality: production
metadata:
  sbom:
    license: Zlib
component_root_path: ./components/device/silabs/si91x/wireless/ble_unified
provides:
- name: ble_unified
source:
- path: src/ble_unified_app.c

template_file:
  - path: templates/ble_init_hook.c.jinja
  - path: templates/ble_unified_app_config.h.jinja
  - path: templates/bt_bitmap.c.jinja

include:
- path: inc
  file_list:
    - path: ble_unified_app.h

template_contribution:
  - name: ble_unified_macros
    value:
      ble_unified_config_macro_name: RSI_BLE_PWR_INX
      ble_unified_config_macro_value: "30"
      ble_unified_config_macro_comment: "BLE power index"
  - name: ble_unified_macros
    value:
      ble_unified_config_macro_name: RSI_BLE_PWR_SAVE_OPTIONS
      ble_unified_config_macro_value: "0"
      ble_unified_config_macro_comment: "BLE power save options"
  - name: ble_unified_macros
    value:
      ble_unified_config_macro_name: ENABLE_NWP_POWER_SAVE
      ble_unified_config_macro_value: "1"
      ble_unified_config_macro_comment: "Enable Network Processor (NWP) power save. Set to 1 to enable BLE and Wi-Fi power save profiles"
  - name: ble_unified_macros
    value:
      ble_unified_config_macro_name: WLAN_TASK_ENABLE
      ble_unified_config_macro_value: "0"
      ble_unified_config_macro_comment: "Enable WLAN task (for coexistence mode). Set to 1 in coex mode, 0 for BLE-only mode"
  - name: ble_unified_macros
    value:
      ble_unified_config_macro_name: PSP_MODE
      ble_unified_config_macro_value: RSI_SLEEP_MODE_2
      ble_unified_config_macro_comment: "Power Save Profile Mode"
  - name: ble_unified_macros
    value:
      ble_unified_config_macro_name: PSP_TYPE
      ble_unified_config_macro_value: RSI_MAX_PSP
      ble_unified_config_macro_comment: "Power Save Profile type"
  - name: ble_unified_bt_bitmap_entries
    value:
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_type: bt_feature_bit_map
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_value: "SL_SI91X_BT_RF_TYPE | SL_SI91X_ENABLE_BLE_PROTOCOL"
  - name: ble_unified_bt_bitmap_entries
    value:
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_type: ble_feature_bit_map
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_value: SL_SI91X_FEAT_BLE_CUSTOM_FEAT_EXTENTION_VALID
  - name: ble_unified_bt_bitmap_entries
    value:
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_type: ble_feature_bit_map
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_value: SL_SI91X_BLE_PWR_INX(RSI_BLE_PWR_INX)
  - name: ble_unified_bt_bitmap_entries
    value:
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_type: ble_feature_bit_map
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_value: SL_SI91X_BLE_PWR_SAVE_OPTIONS(RSI_BLE_PWR_SAVE_OPTIONS)
  - name: ble_unified_bt_bitmap_entries
    value:
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_type: ble_feature_bit_map
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_value: SL_SI91X_916_BLE_COMPATIBLE_FEAT_ENABLE
  - name: agents_slab
    value:
      id: ble_unified
      context: |
        ## BLE Unified Component (Si91x Wireless)
        Top-level orchestration layer for BLE protocol components on Si91x. Provides the BLE task entry point (`rsi_ble_main_app_task`), the protocol initialization sequence, the event loop dispatcher, and power-save management. Application code does NOT call low-level `rsi_ble_*_register_callbacks()` directly; the BLE Unified framework wires every selected protocol component (GAP / SMP / GATT Server / GATT Client / Legacy Adv / Ext Adv) into a single autogenerated init hook chain.
        ### Architecture
        - `ble_unified` is selected by every BLE Unified application; it pulls in `ble`, `ble_unified_framework`, and `cmsis_rtos2`.
        - Every protocol component contributes:
          1. An init function via the `ble_unified_init_hooks` template contribution (called in selection order from `ble_init_hook.c`).
          2. Its `*_config.h` via `ble_unified_config_includes` (autogenerated `ble_unified_app_config.h` aggregates them).
          3. BT/BLE feature-bitmap entries via `ble_unified_bt_bitmap_entries` (autogenerated `bt_bitmap.c`).
          4. Callback wrappers via `wrapper_implementations` and event handler registration via `ble_events`.
        - The autogenerated `ble_unified_app_config.h` provides global runtime knobs: `RSI_BLE_PWR_INX` (BLE power index), `RSI_BLE_PWR_SAVE_OPTIONS`, `ENABLE_NWP_POWER_SAVE`, `WLAN_TASK_ENABLE` (set 1 in coex), `PSP_MODE`, `PSP_TYPE`.
        ### Initialization Sequence (CRITICAL)
        Always follow this exact order in your `app.c`:
        1. `sl_wifi_init()` (with the autogenerated bt_feature_bit_map + ble_feature_bit_map + ble_ext_feature_bit_map applied)
        2. Create the BLE task — its entry point is `rsi_ble_main_app_task` (declared in `ble_unified_app.h`).
        3. From the BLE task, the framework runs every contributed init hook in order, registers all callbacks, then enters the event loop. Do NOT manually call `rsi_ble_gap_register_callbacks()`, `rsi_ble_smp_register_callbacks()`, etc. — they are wrapped by autogenerated registration functions.
        ### Power Save (CoEx)
        - In coex mode set `WLAN_TASK_ENABLE=1` and `ENABLE_NWP_POWER_SAVE=1`.
        - The framework expects WLAN to enter performance profile FIRST, then BLE power save (PSP_MODE / PSP_TYPE). For BLE-only mode set `WLAN_TASK_ENABLE=0`.
        ### Common Mistakes to Avoid
        - Calling `rsi_ble_*_register_callbacks()` from app code — these are owned by the framework wrappers; manual calls overwrite the framework's handlers and break event delivery.
        - Selecting a protocol component (e.g. `gatt_server`) but forgetting `ble_unified` itself — without it, no init hooks run.
        - Editing `ble_unified_app_config.h` before project generation — it is generated from `ble_unified_app_config.h.jinja`; values come from `ble_unified_macros` template contributions and component selections.
    priority: -5302

define:
- name: SLI_SI91X_ENABLE_BLE_UNIFIED

requires:
- name: sl_si91x_wireless
- name: ble
- name: ble_unified_framework
- name: cmsis_rtos2

